 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Recordings in a room with hard floors, mirrors, or tall bookshelves can make things worse. A few simple tricks help. Then let' act on it. A blanket or two on floor absorbs a lot of echo, and cheap one from a dollar store works just fine. Then hang curtains or a thick curtain in front of the fridge and washing machine. They absorb sound nicely. Close the door, and if you can open window bit, do. Open cupboards under the sink help too. Good lab. Let me know how it sounds.",
